# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets.
# Lands at dist/_headers via publicDir; parsed by Workers, never served as an asset.
#
# HSTS is NOT set here. It is owned by the Cloudflare zone (SSL/TLS -> Edge
# Certificates -> HSTS), which is the right home: it also covers redirects and error
# responses that never reach this Worker. Verified that the zone value overrides
# anything set here, so declaring it would be dead config that misleads.
#
# History worth keeping: both HSTS and nosniff were originally assumed to be
# zone-supplied and were therefore omitted. They vanished the instant DNS moved to
# this Worker, which proved the old shared host had been sending them. nosniff is
# still set below because its source is ambiguous — Cloudflare's HSTS panel has an
# optional No-Sniff toggle, and no duplication is observed either way, so keeping it
# is the safe side of the trade.

# Content-hashed by Astro, so the filename changes whenever the bytes do — safe to
# cache forever. Everything else keeps the default `max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which is what HTML wants and yields cheap ETag 304s.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
